## Try it

:::tip Share what you write
**Copy link** puts this whole document in the link, after the `#`. That part of a link is never sent to a server.
:::

Style text with [named colors]{color=blue}, ==highlights== and badges: :badge[Shipped]{color=green} :badge[Beta]{color=amber} · press :kbd[Ctrl+Enter] · progress :progress{value=60}

- [x] Open the playground
- [ ] Break something and check **Diagnostics** :priority[P1] @you
- [ ] Copy a link and open it in a private window

## Diagrams and math

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[Write .smd] --> B{Valid?}
    B -- no --> A
    B -- yes --> C[Share]
```

The area under $x^2$ from 0 to 1:

$$
\int_0^1 x^2\,dx = \frac{1}{3}
$$

## Layout

::::tabs
:::tab npm
```bash
npm install -g styled-markdown
```
:::
:::tab VS Code
```bash
code --install-extension bislink360.styled-markdown
```
:::
::::

```ts title="greet.ts"
export function greet(name: string): string {
  return `Hello, ${name}!`;
}
```

:::decision{status=accepted date=2026-10-01 owner=@you} Keep shared documents in the link
Nothing to host, and nothing stored on a server.
:::

## For agents

:::agent Notes for AI agents
The **Agent view** tab shows what an agent reads: this block is kept, styling is dropped, and headings get line references.
:::
